      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Optional capability of a <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_gradient_enhanced_hypo_elastic" kindref="compound">MaterialGradientEnhancedHypoElastic</ref>: a stress update that also yields the energy tangents. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nNonlocalVariables</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of nonlocal variables of the material.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
A material provides the derivatives of its updated elastic energy density and dissipation wrt the strain increment and the nonlocal variables by inheriting from this class next to <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_gradient_enhanced_hypo_elastic" kindref="compound">MaterialGradientEnhancedHypoElastic</ref>. Elements find the capability with <computeroutput>dynamic_cast</computeroutput> and call this variant instead of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_gradient_enhanced_hypo_elastic_1a529b14adf84be4b6c03afbff4c9dae60" kindref="member">MaterialGradientEnhancedHypoElastic::computeStress</ref> only when they assemble energy gradients. The standard material interface is not affected. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
